# 🛠️ Tools

You only need a few basic tools:

* **Web Browser** — Chrome, Edge, Firefox, etc.
* **Code Editor** — VS Code recommended
* **Git** — Optional at the beginning
* **GitHub** — For saving and sharing projects

---

# 📈 What Comes After HTML?

HTML is only the beginning of web development.

```text
HTML
 ↓
CSS
 ↓
JavaScript
 ↓
Git & GitHub
 ↓
Responsive Web Design
 ↓
Web Projects
 ↓
Frontend Development
```

After completing this roadmap, move on to **CSS** and learn how to turn basic HTML pages into properly designed websites.

---

# 💡 Learning Rule

> **Don't copy code blindly. Understand it, type it, break it, fix it, and build something with it.**

The objective is not to remember every HTML tag.

The objective is to be able to open a blank HTML file and **build something yourself.**

